    <DataNode elementId="AT5G11880-MONOMER" textLabel="Diaminopimelate decarboxylase 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q94A94" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL Diaminopimelate decarboxylase activity was detected from plants in the 60&apos;s. The gene(s) encoding the enzyme has only been recently identified. Arabidopsis contains two diaminopimelate decarboxylase genes, both were able to functionally complement the E. coli lysA mutant.</Comment>
